openWrite [SimTalk]
Opens the XML file, whose content you want to sequentially write to the XMLInterface designated by
<Path>.
Remarks
openWrite applies when you randomly access data.
Note
openWrite encodes the xml file in UTF-8 format. This enables the xml files to be treated as ASCII files
provided only characters from the ASCII character set are used.
Type
Method
Syntax
<Path>.openWrite → boolean
Return Value
The return value has the data type boolean.
Example
MyXMLInterface.filename := "D:\MSXML 4.0\writeSequ.xml"
// opens the XML document for sequential writing
MyXMLInterface.openWrite
MyXMLInterface.startElement("catalog")
MyXMLInterface.startElement("book")
